#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD1333 expect=violation domain=AE
#note "AEDUR (Permissible) is not collected at all, so the bare empty(AEDUR) leaf is TRUE on every row (absent = all-missing, EC-43; Plan B phase 4d' deleted the not var_exists(AEDUR) disjunct that used to make this a separate 'not present' branch): row 1 is RECOVERED/RESOLVED with an empty AEENDTC and no duration anywhere -> fires. Since 2026-09-11 this ALSO pins the R-4.11b gate as Any, not All (T1-30): the present AEENDTC column satisfies Requirements.Variables.Any [AEENDTC, AEDUR], so the verdict is UNCHANGED -- only a dataset with NEITHER column skips (skipped_no_end_columns), and the sister FDA-SD9724 reports that case."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 AESEQ=1
dataset AE class=EVENTS label="Adverse Events"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col AESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col AETERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Adverse Event"
col AEOUT   type=Char label="Outcome of Adverse Event"
col AEENDTC type=Char label="End Date/Time of Adverse Event"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | AE | 01-701-1015 | 1 | HEADACHE | RECOVERED/RESOLVED         | 
CDISCPILOT01 | AE | 01-701-1015 | 2 | RASH     | NOT RECOVERED/NOT RESOLVED | 
